{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04IM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j_U$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0a05ffad32187a76b08c1d571f30267b9a370732b6e5d95d056b31ecdc753591", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d03875e9f9b87c683b1f0414794da2a34443447e7ac95e5ce7aa96d89a43b831", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA fundamental property of an open immersion is\nthat the restriction of the pushforward and the restriction\nof the extension by the empty set produces back the original sheaf.\nThis is not always true for the functors associated to <MATH_0001>\nabove. It is true when <MATH_0002> is a ``subobject of the final object''.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f3ebaf50ee605fcf5b362207ca06bd3fd07490666a735260bdea8d07a38988a3", "unit_id": "tag:04IM:prose-0002"}
